<ContentLayout title="Privacy Policy | TokenCalculator.dev" description="TokenCalculator.dev privacy policy and local-processing commitment." heading="Privacy policy"><p>Your prompts, files, images, tokenization, and document extraction run in your browser. User content is never uploaded to TokenCalculator.dev, Google Analytics, or the public pricing catalog.</p><h2>Analytics choice</h2><p>Google Analytics is optional and loads only after you select “Accept analytics.” It measures page visits, session activity, approximate location, and browser or device information. It never receives prompt text, uploaded files, images, or calculated token counts.</p><p>When accepted, Google Analytics may set first-party cookies beginning with <code>_ga</code>. Your choice is stored locally in your browser. You can review or change it at any time through “Analytics settings” in the footer. Declining or withdrawing consent prevents future analytics collection from this site and removes its analytics cookies where the browser permits.</p><h2>Local browser storage</h2><p>The site uses local browser storage to remember your theme and analytics preference. These settings remain on your device.</p><h2>Local files</h2><p>Document text and image dimensions exist only in the active browser session. Reloading or closing the page removes them.</p><h2>Public model metadata</h2><p>The browser may request public pricing and context-limit data from Models.dev. That request contains no prompt, token count, file, or image data.</p><h2>Hosting logs</h2><p>The hosting provider may retain standard request metadata such as IP address, requested page, and browser user agent. User content is never part of those page requests.</p></ContentLayout>
